,"d":2040},{"n":"ATM","g":"essentials","k":"atm","la":-17.60751,"lo":177.457639,"d":2082},{"n":"Lautoka Jame Masjid","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-17.606111,"lo":177.455,"d":1804,"ds":"The Lautoka Jame Masjid, also known as the Lautoka Jamia Masjid, is a Sunni Islam mosque, located in Lautoka, in the Ba Province, in the Western Division of Fiji.","wpu":"Lautoka Jame Masjid","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/48/Mosque_at_Lautoka%2C_Fiji%2C_1928.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Global Girmit Museum","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-17.641672,"lo":177.420925,"d":4258,"ds":"The Global Girmit Institute (GGI) Museum is co-located with the GGI Library at its headquarters in Saweni, Lautoka, Fiji. Girmit is a corruption of the English word, “agreement” from the indenture agreement the British government made with Indian labourers that consisted of specifics such as the length of stay in Fiji. The labourers came to be known as Girmityas.","wpu":"Global Girmit Museum","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Sugar_cane_is_cut_and_gathered._Auckland_Museum_Creative_Commons.pdf/page1-960px-Sugar_cane_is_cut_and_gathered._Auckland_Museum_Creative_Commons.pdf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Vuda Point","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-17.666667,"lo":177.383167,"d":8819,"ds":"Vuda Point is a headland on the west coast of Viti Levu island, in Ba Province of Fiji. It is located between the towns of Nadi and Lautoka. Vuda Point features the village of Viseisei, with the Vuda Marina yacht harbor and several small resort complexes.","wpu":"Vuda Point","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/59/Viti_Levu_Islands.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Viseisei","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-17.685611,"lo":177.407417,"d":9322,"ds":"Viseisei (Fijian pronunciation: [βisei̯sei̯] ) is a village at Vuda Point on the west coast of Viti Levu island, in Ba Province of Fiji.","wpu":"Viseisei","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/VitiLevu2021OSM.png/960px-VitiLevu2021OSM.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Tivua Island","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-17.614035,"lo":177.344349,"d":9956,"ds":"Tivua Island is an island of the Mamanuca Islands, Fiji. Tivua is a small coral cay located in the northeastern part of the Mamanuca group of islands, northeast of Kadavulailai and Lovuka islands. The island is fringed with white sand and is surrounded by 500 acres (202 hectares) of reef.","wpu":"Tivua Island","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Tivua_Island%2C_Mamanucas_Islands%2C_Fiji%2C_2011.jpg/960px-Tivua_Island%2C_Mamanucas_Islands%2C_Fiji%2C_2011.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Lautoka (Fijian pronunciation: [lɔu̯toka] , Fiji Hindi: लौटोका) is the second largest metropolitan area in Fiji. It is on the west coast of the island of Viti Levu, in the Ba Province of the Western Division. Lying in the heart of Fiji's sugar cane-growing region, the city has come to be known as the Sugar City.","wpu":"Lautoka","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Lautoka-Vitogo-Parade.jpg/960px-Lautoka-Vitogo-Parade.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}